 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Construction of formal proposals",
     "texto": [
      "Within the framework of collegiate resolutions, concertation tables and institutional opinions, recommendations are not presented in the direct imperative but through subordinate dependent clauses introduced by verbs of proposal (**vorschlagen, anregen, empfehlen, fordern**) followed by **dass**: **Die Kommission empfiehlt, dass die Förderkriterien transparent gestaltet werden** (the committee recommends that the aid criteria be designed transparently)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verbal government of dass in proposals",
     "texto": [
      "The subordinating conjunction **dass** systematically moves the conjugated verb to the last position of the clause. In contemporary institutional register, after these verbs the indicative or the passive with a modal is usually used (**gestaltet werden sollen / gestaltet werden müssen**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Main verb",
     "columnas": [
